WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:05.070
- Just one more signature, and whew!

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.290
Our taxes are finally
done. (sighs heavily)

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.657
- Great, what's the damage?

00:00:09.657 --> 00:00:10.740
Huh, not bad.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.140
- Yeah, well, there's one more tax

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.540
that isn't listed on these forms.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.373
- Really?

00:00:16.373 --> 00:00:19.080
- Yeah, and it's one that
every American has to pay,

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.820
even though you rarely think about it.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.520
And it's not only the
government doing the taking,

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.490
our health insurers, our phone companies,

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:29.280
even our employers all get their cut.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.110
- They're cut of what?

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.774
- Your time.

00:00:32.774 --> 00:00:35.357
(upbeat music)

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.070
- The American tax system is
one of the most complicated

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.300
in the developed world,

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.510
and it places a unique
burden on its citizens.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.910
The average American spends 11 hours

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.980
completing all the necessary paperwork,

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.880
and we collectively spend
around $12 billion a year

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:00.000
on tax preparation services and softwares,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.270
not to mention the repercussions
if you get something wrong.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.570
- Journalist Annie Lowrey
calls this the time tax,

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.900
a "levy of paperwork,
aggravation and mental effort

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.610
imposed on citizens..."

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.100
It's the shifting of the
burden of bureaucracy

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.860
from organizations to ordinary people.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.380
And it doesn't just refer to the IRS.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.980
Time taxes are everywhere when
you start looking for them,

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.950
filling out forms at the DMV, time tax.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:29.070
Making multiple phone calls
to get a building permit,

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.030
time tax.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:33.360
Waiting for hours in
line to vote, time tax.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.220
- Now, of course, it's expected

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:38.250
that living in the modern world
will involve some drudgery,

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.230
but if time is money,

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:43.500
it's fair to quantify the
hours we spend on bureaucracy

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.650
and ask whether it's necessary or fair,

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:50.760
especially since the time tax,
unlike our formal tax system

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:55.410
is regressive, meaning the
poorer you are, the more you pay.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:57.990
- If you've never applied
for any safety net programs

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:00.000
like food stamps, housing assistance

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.432
or unemployment benefits,
you might be shocked

00:02:02.432 --> 00:02:05.550
by the number of hoops
you're asked to jump through.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:09.000
Dozens of forms and documents,
in-person interviews,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.700
time sheet logs,
fingerprinting, drug tests

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.620
and intrusive personal questions

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.480
about your career and medical history.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:19.020
And many of these programs
require re-certification,

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:23.160
meaning you have to do it all
over again on a regular basis.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.320
- Adding to the burden is
the fact that poor people

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.570
are less likely to have internet access

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:28.950
and desktop computers

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.530
and more likely to have
frequent changes of address

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.540
and disabilities that may prevent them

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.010
from getting around easily.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.960
If you're already working two jobs

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.610
to barely make ends meet,

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.100
it's a big deal to get time off work

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.370
so you can ride a bus downtown
and wait in line for hours

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.860
to be interrogated by
a government employee.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.816
It's not surprising that
a lot of people instead

00:02:48.816 --> 00:02:52.500
choose to just throw their
hands up and say, "Nevermind."

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.480
- Authors Pamela Herd and Donald Moynihan

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.360
call this phenomenon
administrative burden.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.490
And there's more to it than
just the time and effort

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.810
you put into paperwork,

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:03.450
which they refer to as compliance costs.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.370
- There's also the learning costs

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.440
which are the benefits you miss out on

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.910
because you don't know about them

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:12.270
or can't understand the
complicated application process.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.340
- And there's the psychological costs

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.740
which refers to the humiliation, shame

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.650
or degradation that
applicants must put up with

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:22.590
to access the benefits
they're legally entitled to.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.930
- Now, you might think
that these costs are fair.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.190
Hey, if you want free money,

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:28.830
you're gonna have to put
up with some hassles, okay?

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:32.014
- But remember that Americans
of all socioeconomic levels

00:03:32.014 --> 00:03:34.176
get financial assistance
from the government.

00:03:34.176 --> 00:03:37.200
It's just the programs aimed at the poor

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.200
that seem to treat you
like a convict on parole.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.750
You don't have to pee in
a cup to get a mortgage,

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:45.780
and you don't have to be
fingerprinted to start an IRA.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.420
- Government programs that
tend to have more white, middle

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.040
and upper class beneficiaries

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.550
are typically much easier
to apply for and maintain,

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:55.890
so much so that the people who access them

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:57.870
are more likely to
believe that they're not

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.330
on any kind of government
assistance at all.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:02.970
- There's a long history
of using bureaucracy

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:06.870
to discourage certain undesirable
people from participating

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:07.860
in government.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.720
In response to the 15th amendment

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.480
which gave non-white
men the right to vote,

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.750
many southern states built
bureaucratic roadblocks

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.957
like poll taxes and literacy tests.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.610
- But there are other
less pernicious factors

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:23.040
that underlie the administrative burdens.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:25.020
For one, it saves money.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:27.300
The more people you can
frustrate out of the system,

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.280
the less you have to pay in claims.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.290
As Florida Governor Ron DeSantis said

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.007
about his state's unemployment system,

00:04:33.007 --> 00:04:35.647
"I think the goal was for
whoever designed it was

00:04:35.647 --> 00:04:38.287
"let's put as many kind
of pointless roadblocks

00:04:38.287 --> 00:04:40.927
"along the way so people just
say, oh, the hell with it.

00:04:40.927 --> 00:04:42.420
"I'm not gonna do that."

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.455
- This motivation extends
outside the halls of government.

00:04:45.455 --> 00:04:47.430
Private insurance companies

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:50.580
deliberately make filing
a claim such a hassle

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.850
that some percentage of valid
claimants will just give up.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.280
Automated call centers save money on labor

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.679
by forcing you to spend more
of your time on the phone.

00:04:58.679 --> 00:05:02.730
And employers who used to
automatically pay into pensions

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:06.450
now require their employees
to enroll themselves in 401Ks,

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.970
and many of them never get around to it.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.430
- But some politicians
may actually see a value

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.035
in administrative burden itself.

00:05:13.035 --> 00:05:15.900
If your aim is to shrink
the size of the government,

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:18.360
it can be helpful to
cultivate an impression

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.640
of it as bloated and inefficient.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:21.540
The last thing you want

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:23.340
is for citizens' interactions
with the government

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.140
to be smooth and pleasant.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:26.970
- Of course, the ostensible reason

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:30.030
for administrative burden
is to prevent fraud,

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:30.863
and it is true

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:33.840
there is a not insignificant
amount of fraud and abuse

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:36.060
associated with government benefits.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.880
Hard numbers are very
difficult to come by,

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:43.830
but estimates vary between
5 and 15% of overall payouts

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:46.590
go to people who are
technically ineligible

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:49.320
or are spent on things
they're not intended for.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:51.960
However, a significant
amount of that fraud

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:55.320
is perpetrated by companies
and identity thieves,

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:58.920
not the individuals and families
who genuinely need the help

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:02.070
and are forced to bear the
brunt of administrative burden.

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:03.120
- The ultimate question

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:05.500
is whether preventing
a small amount of fraud

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.461
is worth discouraging
millions of eligible Americans

00:06:08.461 --> 00:06:10.560
from accessing their benefits.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:13.140
Unfortunately, we just don't have the data

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.240
to weigh that question accurately.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:17.639
The amount of time and money
Americans lose to bureaucracy

00:06:17.639 --> 00:06:20.756
has never been comprehensively calculated.

00:06:20.756 --> 00:06:24.113
We don't know how many qualified
Americans skip benefits

00:06:24.113 --> 00:06:25.800
because of red tape,

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:28.140
or whether these massive complex systems

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:31.170
are actually more wasteful
than the fraud itself.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:33.480
- Without this information,
there's little chance

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:36.030
that anything will be done
about administrative burden

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:37.320
in the short term.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:39.960
Fortunately, there are
nonprofit organizations

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.170
dedicated to helping low
income people navigate it.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.150
- And if you happen to be one of the few

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:48.390
who is naturally good at
researching application processes

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:51.540
and filling out forums,
consider yourself lucky.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.520
It's a surprisingly useful skill

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:56.218
in our modern ocean of bureaucracy.

00:06:56.218 --> 00:06:58.096
- [Both] And that's our two cents.

00:06:58.096 --> 00:07:00.540
- [Announcer] Thanks to our patrons

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.270
for keeping "Two Cents"
financially healthy.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:04.650
Click the link in the description

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.052
